        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "312157639c61dcb7f48437abe67ed7f884f739fc",
            "parents": [
                "313d15cf9f14e8a264f97a3370c3be4e494e5e0d"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/45/77545/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                "username": "aravinths1"
            },
            "createdOn": 1768990434,
            "author": {
                "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                "username": "aravinths1"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "package.json",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "I had moved to the standard `<input type=\"date\">` in order to lessen our dependency on bootstrap-vue-next.  Why add yet another npm dependency for this?\n\nBundle size - vue-datepicker-next adds ~15KB"
                },
                {
                    "file": "package.json",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "The native <input type=\"date\"> renders dates based on browser locale and does not guarantee a consistent YYYY-MM-DD format.\n\nSince we require a fixed YYYY-MM-DD format, the datepicker is currently used.\n\nPlease let us know if this is acceptable or if there are alternative suggestions to handle this without an additional dependency."
                },
                {
                    "file": "package.json",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "The current native implementation is good because:\n- The data is always YYYY-MM-DD (what the code processes)\n- Users see dates in their familiar locale format (better UX)\n- The validation already ensures the correct format\n\nIMO, localized input for dates is a better UX.  Is there a requirement to have fixed YYYY-MM-DD format on *input*?  Is it worth 15KB?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "package.json",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "+1 to using `<input type=\"date\">`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "package.json",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "@suryav@ami.com @aravinths@ami.com any updates on this?  Do we need further discussion around `<input type=\"date\">`?"
                }
            ],
